Vita controls: front-touch menus without RmlUi, and gyro aim on by default.

dusk::menu_pointer turns a pointer position into game 2D coordinates by dividing it by the RmlUi
context's size; the Vita has no RmlUi context, so every touch was dropped. set_pointer_surface()
gives that size instead (the Vita passes the game's drawn area, platform/vita/touch.cpp). Nothing
else calls it, and an RmlUi context, when present, still wins, so other platforms are unchanged.
Taps, hit tests and menu handling are Dusklight's own.

game.enableGyroAim defaults to on for the Vita, which always has a gyroscope (SDL's Vita sensor
driver; aiming reads it through Aurora's lib/device.cpp). It stays a user setting: a saved choice
still wins, and the option turns it off.

